    <h2 class="section-heading">The question</h2>
    <div class="section-body">
      <p>Air pollution is one of the leading environmental health risks in European cities. Barcelona, like many dense urban centres, has districts with measurable differences in pollutant levels. This project asks: do the districts with worse air quality also have lower life expectancy?</p>
      <p>Using three pollutants — NO₂, O₃, and PM10 — measured across 10 Barcelona districts in November 2017, and life expectancy data from 2006–2014, I ran a Pearson correlation test to look for a statistical relationship.</p>
